meta {
  name: List Projects
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/project/getAllProjects?page=1&limit=9
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 9
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200 && res.body.data.items.length > 0) {
    bru.setEnvVar('projectId', res.body.data.items[0].id);
    bru.setEnvVar('projectSlug', res.body.data.items[0].slug);
  }
}

docs {
  # List Projects

  Public: **published projects only**, sorted by `order` ascending, then newest
  first, then by `id` so two projects sharing both keys cannot swap places
  between pages. Drafts live behind **List All For Dashboard**.

  **Paginated.** `page` defaults to 1 and `limit` to 9 (max 50); anything below
  1 is a 422. The website renders page one on the server and fetches the rest as
  the visitor scrolls, using `meta.hasMore` to know when to stop.

  Fills the `projectId` and `projectSlug` variables from the first project, so
  the by-id and by-slug requests work straight after this one.

  `projectDetails` is **not** here: no list view renders the long write-up, and
  the website inlines list payloads into its HTML, so it is projected away. Use
  **Get Project** for it.

  `slug` **is** here on purpose — the website's sitemap and JSON-LD build project
  URLs out of list data.

  Links a project does not have (`liveLink`, `frontEndRepo`, `backEndRepo`) are
  left out rather than sent as `""`.

  **Example response**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "1 projects",
    "data": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "…",
          "title": "…",
          "slug": "bari-vara",
          "status": "published",
          "order": 0,
          "summary": "…",
          "frontEndTech": ["Next.js"],
          "backEndTech": ["Express"],
          "liveLink": "https://…",
          "frontEndRepo": "https://…",
          "backEndRepo": "https://…",
          "showOnHomepage": true,
          "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/…/portfolio/projects/….webp",
          "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
        }
      ],
      "meta": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 9,
        "total": 13,
        "totalPages": 2,
        "hasMore": true
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  An empty `image` means that document still holds the pre-Cloudinary buffer —
  run `pnpm migrate:images`. A missing `slug` means `pnpm backfill:slugs` has not
  been run.
}
